Title: 200 AMSTERDAM: THE VERTICAL CITY
Credit: Written for the Screen by
Author: Danny Bouldiez
Episode: PART 00B: WILD HORSE (PROLOGUE)

====

EXT. BROADWAY & 69TH STREET - MORNING

Pedestrians rush past with steaming coffees. Yellow cabs HONK. The relentless tempo of Manhattan.

A young professional checks a notification on her phone, stepping onto the sidewalk without looking down.

SUPER: "Look down. Right now, beneath your feet, there is stone."

INT. SUBTERRANEAN BEDROCK CHAMBER - CONTINUOUS (DUAL STAGE / THEATER VIEW)

Deep beneath the pavement. Cold, damp Manhattan Schist granite. 

High-voltage power conduits, fiber-optic tubes, and ancient iron water mains snake along the sweating rock face.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
You do not think about it. Nobody does. Modern life is an elaborate conspiracy to make you forget the floor beneath civilization.

INT. NEW YORK STATE SUPREME COURT - DAY

Sunlight pours through tall mahogany windows. LAWYERS in $4,000 suits shuffle architectural blueprints.

JUDGE KAUFMAN (60s, sharp, impatient) peers over his glasses.

                         LEAD COUNSEL (STERLING DEV)
          The governing provisions are clear, Your Honor. 
          The development rights have been assembled into a 
          lawful zoning-lot configuration. The Department of 
          Buildings reviewed the structural submissions. The 
          project's height is not a geological question before 
          this court. It is a zoning question, and the zoning 
          question has been answered.

In the back row, ARIS THORNE (50s, disheveled, rumpled trench coat, mud-stained leather satchel) stands up abruptly.

                         ARIS THORNE
          (voice hoarse, vibrating with urgency)
          You can't zone out gravity, Your Honor!

The courtroom turns. Murmurs.

                         JUDGE KAUFMAN
          Sit down, sir, or I'll have the bailiff remove you.

                         ARIS THORNE
          You're anchoring six hundred million pounds of steel 
          and glass into a fracture fault that hasn't seen dynamic 
          shear load in twelve thousand years! The water table under 
          Amsterdam Avenue isn't static—it breathes with the Hudson!

                         LEAD COUNSEL
          Your Honor, Dr. Thorne's credentials have already been 
          reviewed and dismissed by the planning board.

Aris stares at the developers. His eyes burn.

                         ARIS THORNE
          The ground doesn't care about your zoning board. 
          The ground is patient. It remembers everything. 
          And when it speaks... you will listen.

Aris turns and walks out. As his heel hits the marble threshold—

SOUND: A distant, subterranean DULL THUD echoes beneath the courtroom floor.

FADE TO BLACK.
